  "facts": [
    "The Pit River Bridge, officially the Veterans of Foreign Wars Memorial Bridge, stretches 3,588 feet on its upper deck and 2,754 feet below, making it the tallest double‑decked bridge in the United States.",
    "Built in 1942 to replace the submerged Lower Pit River Bridge, it carries Interstate 5 above and a Union Pacific rail line below, a design that emerged during the Shasta Dam construction boom.",
    "In 1954, photographer Virginia Schau captured the dramatic “Rescue on Pit River Bridge,” a moment that earned a Pulitzer Prize for Photography and immortalized the bridge’s rugged beauty."
